cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Is passing a prop-firm challenge evidence of skill? Zero-edge pass rates and the diagnostic value of a pass under ten published rule sets"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Solano Paul"
    given-names: "Sean"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-20"
abstract: "Code, rule tables, simulation results and literature map for a study of retail proprietary-trading evaluations (challenges). A Monte Carlo simulator, validated against 30 closed-form results, is run on the published rules of ten products from eight firms (read 13 October 2026) to measure how often a trader with zero expected profit passes, what a purchase is worth to such a trader, and how much a pass reveals about skill (likelihood ratios and positive predictive value)."
keywords:
  - "proprietary trading"
  - "evaluation challenges"
  - "gambler's ruin"
  - "optional stopping"
  - "likelihood ratio"
  - "screening tests"
  - "retail trading"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bruhmoment2023-real/prop-firm-challenge"
